==Changelog October 23rd==
{{Collapsed section|18|CLICK HERE TO SHOW}}
PSA: As of this week, Game Jam VI is in full swing, and the team will be diving into their passion projects from October 21st to November 1st! This means there will be '''no game update next week on Wednesday, October 30th.'''

'''Halloween 2024 Changes'''

* Marika will now believe you when you claim you’ve heard the cat. To help convince her, we’ve added a third chat option which lets you ''promise'' you heard it.
* Moved a pumpkin in Draynor out of the path of would-be woodcutters.

'''Varlamore: The Rising Darkness Changes'''

* Using the Refiner at the Mastering Mixology minigame whilst wearing Ferocious Gloves will no longer cause hands to stretch. Safety first!
* Clarified the criteria for the Perfect Hueycoatl Combat Achievement.

'''Ironman Status Changes'''

* An important update regarding Ironman accounts:
** Previously, some Ironmen chose to lock their Ironman status 'permanently', worrying that a hijacker might downgrade it behind their back. However, over the years, we've seen an increasing number of Ironmen regret this. Additionally, we now have Jagex Accounts, bringing updated security options to keep hijackers out of the account in the first place. Therefore, as of today's update, the old 'permanent' option is no longer available. If you previously locked your Ironman status permanently and now wish to downgrade, you can do so - provided you have the security of a Jagex Account to protect your status.
** Ironmen who are still concerned about a hijacker downgrading them may choose a downgrade cool-down delay of 90 days. Players whose Ironman status is due to downgrade will receive warnings on login, giving them ample chance to visit the Ironman Tutor in Lumbridge and cancel the change if they don't want it to proceed.

'''Arclight Changes''' 

* Arclight will no longer degrade to Darklight after running out of charges and will instead become an ‘Inactive’ version with the same stats.
* Players can now use one or two Shards at a time to charge Arclight. 333 charges for one Shard, 666 for two, and 1,000 for three.
** You will still require three Shards to upgrade Darklight.
* A warning message will appear in chat when Arclight has 100 charges remaining.
* Repositioned Arclight's Inventory icon to avoid parts being chopped off.

'''Run Energy Changes Beta 2.0'''

* Our Run Energy changes second beta launches tomorrow, '''Thursday October 24th'''! This is your opportunity to test out changes that will impact all game play experiences, so do give it a go.

'''Other Changes'''

* Added a visual indicator to the Tormented Demons which shows when they enter their 100% accuracy phase.
* Examining the murals in the four Pyramid Plunder lobbies reveals how many of each gold chest you’ve looted.
* The Araxyte Slayer Helm now correctly matches your character's skin tone.
* The following weapons and armour from Varlamore have been added to the Supplies chests on PvP Arena worlds:
** Blue Moon armour set and Spear
** Blood Moon armour set
** Eclipse Moon armour set
** Eclipse Atlatl and Atlatl Darts
** Dual Macuahuitl
* Lumberjack Boots are now correctly proportioned to your character.
* You'll no longer find yourself in an unexpected location when using the passageways to exit the Rogues’ Den maze area.
* Fixed a bug causing the Skull Sceptre to forget its autocast setting when switching to another weapon and back again.
* Fixed a bug causing players to teleport a few tiles when standing on the tile directly south of Miss Schism in Draynor Village.
* Clicking Vorkath's Collection Log link no longer sends players to the Whisperer’s page.
* Fixed an issue with the Yanille south Agility shortcut.
* The Venator Ring can no longer be equipped without a Leviathan kill.
* During the Colossal Hydra's special attack, the smaller Hydras are no longer able to attack you.
* While it didn't affect your ability to play the minigame, we have made sure the Kraken's Tentacle is facing the right way during Fishing Trawler.
* The Loot Tracker no longer counts dropped bones twice.
* The Amulet of the Damned's effect now works with the Ahrim's set while manual casting as well as autocasting. Updated the set effect wording to reflect this change.
* When you use 250 Firelighters to unlock a new colourway for your Phoenix pet, you will now have permanent access to that colour. After unlocking once, you can then freely use the 'Metamorphosis' option on the pet to change it.
* We know there are some very dedicated fans of the Old Torva outfit, and while we currently aren't adding it to the game itself, this week we've added the files to the config. This means that RuneLite will now be able to utilise the file and give you the option to don the OG style for your own enjoyment. It's important to know that when activating it via the FashionScape plugin, the outfit will only be visible to you. The armour pieces are unavailable in the main game and are therefore untradeable, can't be sold or bought at the GE and will not leave placeholders in your Bank.
* Fixed a Farming issue where curing a diseased herb could cause it to transform into a different kind of herb altogether.
* Fixed an issue where the judge in King's Ransom appeared to have a beard but no head.
* Added the Last Contract option when using NPC Contact, which will allow players to talk to Amy about Mahogany Homes contracts.
* Enabled spectators scrying into the Theatre of Blood to be visible in the three waves previously exempt from this, meaning fighters will be able to see their audience. Public chat will be available between the fighters and spectators in the following fights:
** Nylocas
** Xarpus
** Verzik
* The latest Deadman Mode Rug item has been tweaked to make the skulls much clearer.

'''PvP Rota'''

The PvP rota has moved to '''Period B''':

* 560 - (UK) - PvP World
* 319 - (US) - Bounty Hunter World
* 579 - (US) - High-Risk PvP World
* 561 - (UK) - Free-to-Play PvP World
* 580 - (US) - LMS Competitive

World 390 (AUS) for LMS Competitive has been <u>'''de-activated'''</u> with this rota.

World 569 (AUS) for Bounty Hunter has been <u>'''de-activated'''</u> with this rota.

The PvP Arena is using '<b>Zerker</b>' loadouts in Ranked Duels and Tournaments this week.

