==Ironman Status Changes==
This week also brings an important update for Ironmen.

Previously, some Ironmen chose to lock their Ironman status 'permanently', worrying that a hijacker might downgrade it behind their back. However, over the years, we've seen an increasing number of Ironmen regret this. Additionally, we now have Jagex Accounts, bringing updated security options to keep hijackers out of the account in the first place. Therefore, as of today's update, the old 'permanent' option is no longer available. If you previously locked your Ironman status permanently and now wish to downgrade, you can do so - provided you have the security of a Jagex Account to protect your status.

Ironmen who are still concerned about a hijacker downgrading them may choose a downgrade cool-down delay of 90 days. Players whose Ironman status is due to downgrade will receive warnings on login, giving them ample chance to visit the Ironman Tutor in Lumbridge and cancel the change if they don't want it to proceed.

==Arclight Changes==
After the addition of While Guthix Sleeps, Arclight gained a new feature which allowed players to infuse spent'' ''charges to count towards the 10,000-charge total required to upgrade it to Emberlight. However, when Arclight depleted to 0 charges, it automatically downgraded to Darklight, which meant your infusion progress was lost.

Following your feedback, running out of charges will now create an ‘Inactive’ version of the Arclight, which remains usable in combat with the same stats as Darklight and maintains your infusion progress.

While we were at it, we also made some additional improvements:

* Players can now use one or two Shards at a time to charge Arclight. 333 charges for one Shard, 666 for two, and 1,000 for three.
** You will still require three Shards to upgrade Darklight.
* A warning message will appear in chat when Arclight has 100 charges remaining.
* Repositioned Arclight's Inventory icon to avoid parts being chopped off.

==Run Energy Changes Beta 2.0==
Our second Run Energy changes beta launches tomorrow, '''Thursday October 24th'''! This is your opportunity to test out changes that will impact all game play experiences, no matter what you get up to in Gielinor.

For all the details on what these changes are and how to take part in the beta, keep your eye out for a dedicated Run Energy Changes blog on the day.

==Game Jam VI==
[[File:Halloween Fixes & Miscellaneous Changes (2).jpeg|thumb|600px|center|''If you can't see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2024/newsposts/2024-10-23/Game_Jam6.jpeg here].'']]

As we've stepped into the final quarter of the year, it's time for another Game Jam!

Game Jams are internal events that we run twice a year, providing us with a fantastic opportunity to come together as a team and pursue passion projects outside the normal roadmap. Previous Game Jams have introduced projects that eventually became Scurrius, Perilous Moons, the Wilderness updates, Project Rebalance, and more!

With our sixth Game Jam in full swing, the team will be diving into their passion projects from October 21st to November 1st. This means there will be '''no game update next week, on Wednesday, October 30th.'''

J-Mods will be using the '''#OSRSGameJam''' hashtag on X to share what they've been cooking - so if you want to see what we’re up to this time, make sure to check it out!

Likewise, there will also be a dedicated #Game-Jam-VI channel on [http://discord.gg/OSRS our Discord server], where some J-Mods will be sharing their ideas and soliciting your feedback!

==Discord Activities==
===J-Mod Activity===
[[File:Halloween Fixes & Miscellaneous Changes (3).png|thumb|400px|center|''If you can't see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2024/newsposts/2024-10-23/JMod_prophunt.jpg here].'']]

Is it a tree, or is it a J-Mod? There’s only one way to find out!

We know you lot love hide and seek, so we're hosting a '''J-Mod Prop Hunt''' event on [http://discord.gg/OSRS our official Discord server] this weekend! On Sunday, J-Mods will disguise themselves as props across Gielinor, and it's up to you and your fellow ‘Scapers to find them! We'll be dropping clues in the''' #F2P-Clues''' and '''#Members-Clues''' channels under the Events category on the day. Then it’s up to you to head to the right location and see what your favourite J-Mods have transformed into!

Everyone will meet in Varrock Square to kick off the event. Make sure you're in the event discussion channels in the Discord server if you plan to take part!

This is your official save the date:

* This Sunday, October 27th
* 19:00 BST
* Members World 358 | Free-to-Play World 500
* Meeting point: Varrock Square

See you there!

We work alongside our Discord Volunteer Moderators to help provide you with activities and events that you can take part in. For the past couple of months, our moderators have been hard at work organising and running events both in and out of game via the server. We've had J-Mod events, player-led activities and games hosted by our mod team themselves! The team are dedicated to bringing you the activities that you want to take part in, so felt it was high time we got your feedback on what they’ve put on so far, and what you want to see in the future. So, we would love it if you could take a couple of minutes to fill this in and let the mod team know your thoughts!

===Discord Stages===
[[File:Halloween Fixes & Miscellaneous Changes (4).png|thumb|400px|center|''If you can't see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2024/newsposts/2024-10-23/JMods_Draw.jpg here].'']]

We're excited to announce our next Discord Stage call!

On '''Tuesday, October 29th at 16:00 GMT''', Mod Blossom will be joined by Mod Jerv (Concept Artist) and Mod Skylark (Character Artist) to chat about art in Old School while Mod Jerv live-draws your suggestions! We've opened up a new channel to gather your drawing ideas early, so Mod Skylark can mock some of them up in 3D to show off during the stages. Head to the ''Drawing Suggestions'' channel to start suggesting what you'd like to see created! Please bear in mind that this Stages is just for fun, and not to develop in-game items, which means you can go wild with your ideas and get creative. We can't wait to see what you come up with! We'll be opening our Ask Your Questions channel on the day of the Stages, too, so prepare any art-related questions you have and pop them in there.

